@description Rea-Sixty
@author Frank Acklin
@version 0.1.31
@changelog
  - Codename: 60% of the time, it works every time.
  - Fix: FX-Learn params on JSFX plug-ins no longer slam to an extreme — driven as continuous with a sub-linear accel curve; UF8 V-Pots and UC1 encoders now feel identical on the same param
  - Fix: Fine mode (Shift) keeps working on coarse JSFX sliders — sub-step moves accumulate until the value advances
  - New: FX Learn → Advanced sensitivity goes down to 0.01 (typeable value box); Device speed minimum lowered to 0.10
  - Fix: UC1 CHANNEL-encoder scroll no longer leaves the 7-seg / LCD counting up after a fast flick — display jumps straight to the landed track
  - New: UF8 bank-scroll stride (Settings → Bindings → UF8) — scroll past the surface edge by 8 (next bank) or by 1 channel
